# Untracked local developer state. `Dockerfile` does `COPY backend/ backend/`,
# and `settings.py` calls `load_dotenv(backend/.env, override=False)` at
# import — so without these two rules a developer's real GEMINI_API_KEY,
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY, AGENT_RUNTIME_API_KEY or CSRF_SECRET would be baked into
# the image and loaded inside every container for each key compose does not
# set. They would also make the recorded image digest a function of untracked
# local state, which defeats NFR21's "reproducible from reviewed
# infrastructure code". `.gitignore` ignores exactly these paths, and
# `frontend/.dockerignore` already excluded `.env*`.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/var/
*.db
